_id": "toolu_012NUc3doh4WybS2t5ao38rz", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 12587, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01WiY6zNHPmjJLw3RHhatwG9", "tool": "trigger_ci", "args": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-fin-212-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 12887, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WiY6zNHPmjJLw3RHhatwG9", "tool": "trigger_ci", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-fin-212-08d3cd5986", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 12887, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WiY6zNHPmjJLw3RHhatwG9", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 14730, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01ESi71FYHS6uYgZAj2CNK5K", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "args": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "max_wait_s": 900, "confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 372887, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01ESi71FYHS6uYgZAj2CNK5K", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 372887, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01ESi71FYHS6uYgZAj2CNK5K", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 378150, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Bg46xqsvGMRDbaiw49EyPD", "tool": "open_pr", "args": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "## Summary\n`round_money` in `src/money.py` was documented as using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. This caused `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (e.g. `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`).\n\n## Change\n- Switch the `quantize` rounding mode from `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (and update the import).\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986`: **passed**.\n\nNote: this changes rounding behavior for exact half-cent values (e.g. x.xx5 where the preceding digit is even now rounds down). This is the intended behavior per FIN-212.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 409050, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Bg46xqsvGMRDbaiw49EyPD", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 409050, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Bg46xqsvGMRDbaiw49EyPD", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 411569, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01K48vpZunSoC5jCxuwuuZH6", "tool": "request_review", "args": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.9}, "confidence": 0.9}, {"t_ms": 411869, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01K48vpZunSoC5jCxuwuuZH6", "tool": "request_review", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 411869, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01K48vpZunSoC5jCxuwuuZH6", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 416850, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and pull request #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That's why 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed that function to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. It's a one-file change, in commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). When I opened it, the reviewer list came back empty, so I requested alex separately and that request went through.\n\nI haven't merged it. Under policy, merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\n**Behavior change:** amounts that land exactly on a half cent will now round to the nearest even cent, so some round down instead of up (2.665 becomes 2.66). FIN-212 calls for this, but any code that relied on the old rounding will get different results. I noted this in the PR.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the repository and the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01QXk2gbVVioMfEQ6nbcGGAC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014AnweLPD9VHQ39Adfe2EUq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012bBUbCrpzWbzVHApHLUgQS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: the code uses `ROUND_HALF_UP` while the docstring and tests require `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Creating a branch for the fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CkiVuxeHq2KiCkqMnr2G5t", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012NUc3doh4WybS2t5ao38rz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money, per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WiY6zNHPmjJLw3RHhatwG9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-fin-212-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01ESi71FYHS6uYgZAj2CNK5K", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "max_wait_s": 900, "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on commit 08d3cd5986. Opening the pull request now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Bg46xqsvGMRDbaiw49EyPD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "## Summary\n`round_money` in `src/money.py` was documented as using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. This caused `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (e.g. `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`).\n\n## Change\n- Switch the `quantize` rounding mode from `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (and update the import).\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986`: **passed**.\n\nNote: this changes rounding behavior for exact half-cent values (e.g. x.xx5 where the preceding digit is even now rounds down). This is the intended behavior per FIN-212.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR was opened, but its reviewer list came back empty, so I'll request alex directly.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01K48vpZunSoC5jCxuwuuZH6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and pull request #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That's why 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed that function to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. It's a one-file change, in commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). When I opened it, the reviewer list came back empty, so I requested alex separately and that request went through.\n\nI haven't merged it. Under policy, merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\n**Behavior change:** amounts that land exactly on a half cent will now round to the nearest even cent, so some round down instead of up (2.665 becomes 2.66). FIN-212 calls for this, but any code that relied on the old rounding will get different results. I noted this in the PR.", "type": "text"}]}]}